 "f1OldTexts": {
  "a": {
   "text": "8 test or test-support files",
   "inR1Body": 1,
   "inR2Body": 0
  },
  "b": {
   "text": "3. The no-write row now reads destructuring targets: `[Object.freeze] = […]` (U4), `({ value: Object.freeze } = …)` (U5), and property targets inside parentheses, defaults and spreads.",
   "inR1Body": 1,
   "inR2Body": 0
  },
  "c56": {
   "text": "5. A workspace package whose `exports` or `main` target contains `/../` now throws. Both root-alias rows fail on it (E4, below). Before, `./dist/x/../index.js` was joined to `src/index.ts` and accepte",
   "inR1Body": 1,
   "inR2Body": 0
  },
  "d": {
   "text": "7. A package entry the config does not alias, other than the six listed, fails. That covers a new export added without a root alias, and an existing alias removed.",
   "inR1Body": 1,
   "inR2Body": 0
  },
  "e": {
   "text": "and lists the six entries the config leaves to their built dist:",
   "inR1Body": 1,
   "inR2Body": 0
  }
 },
 "f1b": {
  "rawText": "3. The no-write row now reads destructuring targets: `[Object.freeze] = […]` (U4), `({ value: Object.freeze } = …)` (U5), and property targets inside parentheses, spreads and nested patterns. A property target with a default (`[Object.freeze = f] = []`) was already refused at `1a8864d9`, because the default is itself a property assignment.",
  "inR2Body": 1,
  "nbsp": 0
 },
 "f1c": {
  "rawText": "5. A workspace package whose `exports` or `main` target contains `/../` now throws, in any condition, `types` included. Before, an entry whose conditions all name `./dist/x/../state-directory.js` was joined to `src/state-directory.ts` and accepted; both root-alias rows and the whole S10 file now fail on it. E4, below, changes the `import` condition alone, so its conditions disagree and the unreadable-entry throw refused it at `1a8864d9` too: it shows the new message, not a new refusal.",
  "inR2Body": 0,
  "nbsp": 0
 },
